<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Audience fit</p>
    <h2 class="section-title">Virginia moms, and every mom watching them go.</h2>
    <div class="mk-fit">
      <div>
        <h3>Who she is</h3>
        <p>A solo mom in her 30s traveling with her kids, or taking the trip on her own. Solo describes the trip, not her marital status: she may be divorced, widowed, a military spouse with a partner stationed overseas, or partnered with someone who will not go outside. Her kids are her world, and she does life with them instead of watching from the sidelines.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>How she buys</h3>
        <p>She is independent, bold, and pre-sold on the desire to go. What stops her is logistics overwhelm, not price. She makes most buying decisions in her household, her splurge is travel, and every destination I feature is framed by drive time from Virginia, where my core audience plans its road trips.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mk-reported" style="text-align: left; margin-top: 1rem;">Over 80% women ages 29 to 44. Core audience in Virginia and the DC drive market, expanding across the East Coast and the USA. Instagram community: 83.7% women, 98% United States, with top follower cities Washington DC, Virginia Beach, and Richmond.</p>
  </div>
